# PART 3. DESIGN AND USER EXPERIENCE

## 3.1 Design philosophy

The system must be extremely simple, professional and user-friendly.

Many hotel employees are not technical.

Use:

- Large readable text.
- Large touch-friendly buttons.
- Clear icons with labels.
- Simple forms.
- Dropdown menus.
- Date pickers.
- Number pads for amounts.
- Short instructions.
- Clear confirmation messages.
- Simple dashboard cards.
- Search and filters.
- Minimal navigation.

A normal employee should complete a common task within three taps wherever practical.

Avoid unnecessary complexity.

## 3.2 Responsive design

Support:

- Android smartphones.
- iPhones.
- Tablets.
- Desktop computers.
- Laptop computers.

Mobile-first design is mandatory.

On desktop, use a professional sidebar and wider reporting tables.

On mobile, use simple navigation, large cards and compact forms.

## 3.3 Visual identity

Use a professional SEAM visual identity.

Suggested design:

- Primary: Deep navy or dark green.
