# PART 7. GLOBAL BUSINESS AND FINANCIAL RULES

These rules apply to all seven phases.

1. Never hardcode an individual hotel's identity.
2. Never hardcode hotel room numbers or employee names.
3. Never hardcode selling prices, tax rates or service charges.
4. Make operational settings configurable.
5. Use a single source of truth for financial transactions.
6. Use reusable calculation functions.
7. Preserve historical financial information.
8. Every approval must identify the approving user.
9. Every important transaction must have a reference number.
10. Every closed report must have a traceable history.
11. Every dashboard must use real database data.
12. Never silently change historical transactions.
13. Use role-based permissions on both frontend and backend.
14. Never expose secret credentials in frontend code.
15. Keep each hotel's information isolated.
16. Do not allow subscription restrictions to destroy hotel data.
17. Do not allow unauthorized users to export confidential reports.
18. All modules must work on mobile and desktop.

